0..79 Comment "//! Corten\'s running example as THIR written by hand, its postcondition derived"
80..118 Comment "//! in a weakest-precondition calculus"
119..200 Comment "//! [Farka-2026-corten_foundational_verification_rust_programs], 2026, § 4, Fig."
201..279 Comment "//! 2: `example` returns early from inside `identity`\'s argument. The calculus"
280..352 Comment "//! is the specification monad of THIR\'s control effect: an expression\'s"
353..432 Comment "//! precondition takes one postcondition for the value it ends at and one for a"
433..504 Comment "//! `return`, a `return` sends its operand\'s value to the second, and a"
505..575 Comment "//! function\'s guard, the effect\'s handler, hands both to the caller\'s"
576..657 Comment "//! continuation (§ 4.2, Defs. 4.1, 4.2 and 4.10). Departing from § 4: `break`,"
658..732 Comment "//! `continue` and `nomatch` are left out, `u8` is read as `Integer`, each"
733..813 Comment "//! function takes one parameter, and propositions are read as types. The axioms"
814..888 Comment "//! are written twice. As the rules of `Thir.Wp`, over THIR\'s nodes as its"
889..968 Comment "//! operations, the checker orients them, joins their pairs in the second-order"
969..1046 Comment "//! reading, and fires them at an inspected call: `example`\'s guarded body at"
1047..1126 Comment "//! false ends at its return continuation, never reaching `identity`. As a fold"
1127..1203 Comment "//! of THIR\'s data, the normaliser computes each precondition and the kernel"
1204..1275 Comment "//! replays it, so `example` meets its specification at every value and"
1276..1313 Comment "//! postcondition given `identity`\'s."
1314..1317 Comment "//!"
1318..1390 Comment "//! - cites: [Farka-2026-corten_foundational_verification_rust_programs]"
1391..1394 Comment "//!"
1395..1559 Comment "//! [Farka-2026-corten_foundational_verification_rust_programs]: https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.04372 \"Farka et al., Corten: Foundational Verification of Rust Programs\""
